to\n\n$$\n10(5R+4V).\n$$\n\nThis is $10$ times the cost of a single bouquet. Thus, the factor $10$ must be the total number of bouquets that Joseph purchased."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a926bb0a-acd8-529c-8705-f6c7b4bbc2c2" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing an Expression With a Constant Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c406a0f-af31-5af6-99df-d3dc091819a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15(P+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494345} {:answer/id #uuid "3997a93d-5a41-5663-8d38-470dc7a8f828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494438} {:answer/id #uuid "92913609-8371-5fb8-b553-76afa675c073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P+15P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494650} {:answer/id #uuid "becae382-922a-538d-a88a-8010c37df62e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15P+P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494763} {:answer/id #uuid "bf2ae639-7aba-53cf-9684-cc8c1115b541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf2ae639-7aba-53cf-9684-cc8c1115b541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494768} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae26588-3055-5b2b-8fae-e3af9eb41e65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a52234c2-10d3-5f1e-bf78-705f84575746" :question/math-academy-id "q-44815" :question/problem "Paul is buying a cell phone at an online store. The price of the cell phone is $P$ dollars, and Paul also has to pay $$15$ for the shipping and handling of the product.\n\nWhat expression represents the total cost, in dollars, of the cell phone?" :question/worked-solution "The price of the cell phone is $P$ dollars.  \n\nThe amount for shipping and handling is $$15.$\n\n Hence, Paul's total bill for the cell phone will be $P+15$ dollars."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133851 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a696afb-6edc-5445-a6e4-23b82f96c76b" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting an Expression With Multiple Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d5cee32-6e9f-59a4-aabb-e7a461e0f774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Each small pizza costs $$3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494543} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac2f850-63dd-5fd8-b6fc-4903951c7324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Kate has purchased $3M$ medium drinks in total" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494672} {:answer/id #uuid "a8eeae1a-9a77-510d-8565-6cea9fd82a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Each medium drink costs $$3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494707} {:answer/id #uuid "b5da7c72-ce33-58f8-a230-521f31aafe24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The total number of medium drinks that Kate purchased" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494741} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3e3a82-a892-5c25-9f44-4e2fe9aee571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Kate has purchased $M$ medium drinks in total" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5da7c72-ce33-58f8-a230-521f31aafe24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The total number of medium drinks that Kate purchased" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494741} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8781f3-146c-58fd-b134-089f69cd061b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5846d998-51e9-574a-9a51-5526adf86d55" :question/math-academy-id "q-45109" :question/problem "A small pizza costs $S$ dollars and a medium drink costs $M$ dollars. Kate is purchasing some pizzas and drinks for her family and the total bill comes to $6S+3M$ dollars. \n\nWhat does the factor $3$ mean in this context?" :question/worked-solution "A small pizza costs $S$ dollars and a medium drink costs $M$ dollars.\n\nKate's bill, in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n6S+3M.\n$$\n\nHence, the factor $3$ must be the total number of medium drinks that Kate purchased."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a926bb0a-acd8-529c-8705-f6c7b4bbc2c2" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing an Expression With a Constant Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9167d26-3b50-5780-831a-48b1b2e8ddcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132956} {:answer/id #uuid "24f670c1-ee74-56bf-ad2c-ba4cc0b2b85c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132959} {:answer/id #uuid "36fcf1e8-a22a-517c-abc5-7a70a42ef00f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15n+3n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494432} {:answer/id #uuid "87dd191d-0ea0-5d3b-ae24-7e204ca5aaac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3n+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494618} {:answer/id #uuid "c95a2671-29b2-5fbd-9631-c123bec1c154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15n+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87dd191d-0ea0-5d3b-ae24-7e204ca5aaac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3n+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494618} :answer-field/id #uuid "68de4bff-9a2b-5bd7-b567-4fa2f26a643d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b732ae55-1e03-5b4b-a75c-931094700bbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-57508" :question/problem "A pizzeria charges $$15$ for a cheese pizza and $$3$ for each topping.\n\nWhat expression gives the total cost, in dollars, of a pizza with $n$ toppings?" :question/worked-solution "If $n$ is the number of toppings, and the pizzeria charges $$3$ per topping, then the cost for $n$ toppings must be $3n.$ \n\nHowever, there is also a fixed fee for the cheese pizza. This fee is $$15.$ Consequently, the constant term of the expression should be $15.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of a pizza with $n$ toppings is:\n\n$$\n3n+15\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133947 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "758ce589-dcf8-5be8-8f15-ae72172050db" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing an Expression With a Tax Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165fc77c-ab41-5d18-acce-d06f1b851a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T+0.9T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494360} {:answer/id #uuid "43100444-737d-5eeb-a3b6-f25b570f66a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T-0.09T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494454} {:answer/id #uuid "47509097-65c5-5033-8c14-e8eef3e5c195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T+0.09T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494459} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8792ba-d801-55c9-a043-a1b1edcefbbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T+0.09" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494535} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0b0ac7-57a5-5649-b7e7-a5c51bcfd6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.09T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47509097-65c5-5033-8c14-e8eef3e5c195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T+0.09T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494459} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab5d524-2b50-5c5a-b48c-e9ea4678be8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9076f1fb-4181-58aa-adca-483a1b65f8fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-75774" :question/problem "Sophie reserves a hotel room. The price of the room is $T$ dollars and, additionally, she must pay a $9%$ luxury tax.\n\nWhich expression gives the total cost, in dollars, of the hotel room after tax is applied?" :question/worked-solution "The price before taxes of a hotel room is $T$ dollars.\n\nThe amount of taxes Sophie pays is  $9%$ of the price of the hotel room, or $0.09T.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the  hotel room after luxury tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nT+0.09T\n$$"}]}
